1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,740
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:04,500
Last time, I said the family works the other way round.

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:08,080
Today, we learn the family trick for taking away.

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,020
But first, a puzzle.

5
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,360
Eleven take away six.

6
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,220
Make eleven.

7
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:19,220
One lower bead on the ones rod, and one lower bead on the tens rod.

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,220
Thumb pushes them up.

9
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,520
Six's friend is four.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,580
The big friend says: add four to the ones rod, then take ten off the tens rod.

11
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:30,800
Quick guess.

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,340
Is there room for four more lower beads on the ones rod?

13
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:37,780
Nope!

14
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,260
Only three fit.

15
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:40,460
Whoa.

16
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,120
The big friend is stuck.

17
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:44,600
Why?

18
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:49,060
The upper bead is up, and the lower beads are almost full.

19
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:50,920
No room to add four.

20
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,280
Who can help?

21
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,240
The small friend!

22
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,460
Four's small friend is one.

23
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:02,380
To add four: take away one, then add five.

24
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,920
The big friend and the small friend, side by side.

25
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,140
That team is called the family.

26
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,200
Here is our routine.

27
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:10,940
Look.

28
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:11,880
Call.

29
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:12,640
Move.

30
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,320
Look: room on the ones rod?

31
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,560
Call: no room, call the family.

32
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:21,100
Move: ones rod first.

33
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,500
The big friend says: minus six equals plus four, minus ten.

34
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,320
The small friend swaps plus four for minus one, plus five.

35
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:38,580
So the family says: minus six equals minus one, plus five, minus ten.

36
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:41,920
Why?

37
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,700
Minus ten takes four too many.

38
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,900
So we add four back first.

39
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,360
Now remember last time.

40
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,240
Plus six was plus one, minus five, plus ten.

41
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,820
What changed today?

42
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:58,980
Every sign flipped!

43
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:00,160
It is a mirror.

44
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:03,420
So which finger now, thumb or index?

45
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:07,440
Index finger!

46
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:08,960
Adding went up.

47
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:10,900
Taking away goes down.

48
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,480
Up is the thumb.

49
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,220
Down is the index finger.

50
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:16,620
Move.

51
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,600
Lower beads first, then the upper bead.

52
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:20,860
Minus one.

53
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,780
The lower bead goes down.

54
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,360
Plus five.

55
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,260
The upper bead goes down.

56
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,000
Tens rod last.

57
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,840
One bead goes down.

58
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:30,920
Boom!

59
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,620
Eleven take away six is five.

60
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:38,220
Next: twenty-two take away seven.

61
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:39,220
Make it.

62
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:44,060
Two lower beads on the ones rod, and two lower beads on the tens rod.

63
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:45,180
Thumb up!

64
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:46,300
Look.

65
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:48,200
Seven's friend is three.

66
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,120
Room for three more lower beads?

67
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:53,800
No!

68
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,180
Just two fit.

69
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,080
Call.

70
00:02:56,860 --> 00:03:00,580
Minus seven equals minus two, plus five, minus ten.

71
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:03,960
Move.

72
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,300
Minus two.

73
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,140
Two lower beads go down.

74
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,400
Now plus five.

75
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:10,740
Upper bead down.

76
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:12,260
Tens rod.

77
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:13,920
One bead goes down.

78
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,020
Index finger, every time!

79
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:16,780
Boom!

80
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:19,340
Twenty-two take away seven is fifteen!

81
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,980
Mirror fans, tap like!

82
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:26,000
And subscribe, the next trick is a big one.

83
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:27,400
Minus eight.

84
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:28,800
Make ninety-three.

85
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,700
On the ones rod, three lower beads.

86
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:35,880
Then on the tens rod, four lower beads and the upper bead.

87
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:39,420
Thumb for the lower beads, index finger for the upper bead.

88
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:40,380
Look.

89
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,340
Eight's friend is two.

90
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,480
How many more lower beads fit?

91
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,360
Only one!

92
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:49,080
Call.

93
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:53,340
Minus eight equals minus three, plus five, minus ten.

94
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:56,720
Move.

95
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,080
Minus three.

96
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,960
Three lower beads go down.

97
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,180
Then plus five.

98
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,000
Down goes the upper bead.

99
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,500
Tens rod.

100
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,000
One bead goes down.

101
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:07,840
Boom!

102
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,560
Ninety-three take away eight is eighty-five!

103
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:12,500
Flip it.

104
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,960
Plus family: up, thumb.

105
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:18,060
Minus family: down, index finger.

106
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:22,960
Plus family: plus lower beads, minus five, plus ten.

107
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:27,960
Minus family: minus lower beads, plus five, minus ten.

108
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,240
Same numbers.

109
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:30,500
Mirror moves.

110
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:37,780
Minus six, minus seven, minus eight, minus nine.

111
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,480
Four mirror formulas.

112
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,060
Your go.

113
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:42,320
Make eighty-four.

114
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:44,900
On the ones rod, four lower beads.

115
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,760
Then on the tens rod, three lower beads and the upper bead.

116
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:49,840
Choose your fingers!

117
00:04:50,770 --> 00:04:51,100
Look.

118
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,880
What is nine's friend?

119
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:56,380
One!

120
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,840
Check the ones rod.

121
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,380
Four lower beads already.

122
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,880
No room at all!

123
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:01,700
Call.

124
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,100
Nine is five and four more.

125
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,460
So how many lower beads come off first?

126
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:09,960
Four!

127
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:14,100
Minus nine equals minus four, plus five, minus ten.

128
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:16,460
Move.

129
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:19,020
All down, so all index finger.

130
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:20,400
Ones rod first.

131
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,860
What number is showing now?

132
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:29,280
Eighty-four take away nine is seventy-five!

133
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:30,780
Mirror master!

134
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:34,080
You did Look, Call, Move all by yourself.

135
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:37,380
Try Look, Call, Move on your own abacus.

136
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,920
Get Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

137
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:41,880
It is free.

138
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:43,220
See you next time!
